807: ## 9. Edge Cases, Pitfalls & Failure Modes
808: 
809: The following table documents 14 specific edge cases identified during the survey and the exact design behavior implemented across all exporters:
810: 
811: | # | Domain | Edge Case / Condition | Failure Mode If Handled Naively | Required Exporter Behavior |
812: |---|---|---|---|---|
813: | 1 | CSV | Field contains comma `,` or quote `"` | Corrupts column count and misaligns table cells | Wrap field in `"..."`, escape internal quotes as `""` per RFC 4180 § 2.7. |
814: | 2 | CSV | Host OS configured to European locale (comma decimal `,`) | Outputs `47,606212` which splits latitude into two separate columns | Explicitly format using invariant culture (`.`). Never rely on default locale formatting. |
815: | 3 | CSV | Missing / zero start timestamp | Formats bogus date or panics | Fall back to elapsed flight time from zero ($t = 0.000\text{ s}$) with `1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z`. |
816: | 4 | KML | Coordinate ordering `latitude,longitude,altitude` | Reversing coordinate order places path on antipodal quadrant in Google Earth | Strictly emit `longitude,latitude,altitude` order in all `<coordinates>`. |
817: | 5 | KML | Web color `#RRGGBB` used directly in `<color>` | Color order inverted: `#FF0000` (Red) renders as Blue in Google Earth | Convert RGB to KML hex order: `AABBGGRR` (`Alpha + Blue + Green + Red`). |
818: | 6 | KML | Multi-segment coloring without repeating boundary vertex | Google Earth renders visual gaps/tears between segment $N$ and segment $N+1$ | Duplicate boundary vertex $P_{\text{split}}$ as the final point of segment $N$ and first point of $N+1$. |
819: | 7 | KML | Drone hovering stationary for 10 minutes at 10 Hz (6,000 points in $0.5\text{ m}$) | Massive polygon thrashing and GPU stall in Google Earth | Filter stationary hover jitter ($\Delta d < 0.15\text{ m}$) before emission. |
820: | 8 | KML | Fill transparency set to 100% (invisible) | Emitting `<extrude>1</extrude>` creates invisible extrusion overhead | Omit `<extrude>1</extrude>` completely when fill alpha is 0. |
821: | 9 | GPX | Emitting local time or missing `Z` suffix in `<time>` | Third-party GPX parsers (Garmin, Strava) reject track for schema violation | Strictly emit ISO 8601 UTC timestamp ending in `Z` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.fffZ`). |
822: | 10 | GPX | Negative elevation in below-sea-level depressions (e.g. $-86\text{ m}$) | Clamping to zero corrupts valid terrain altitude | Format signed float `{:.2}`; schema allows signed elevations in `<ele>`. |
823: | 11 | GeoJSON | Emitting custom `crs` member | Violates RFC 7946 § 4 which deprecated custom CRS | Do not emit `crs` member; use default WGS84 CRS84 datum strictly. |
824: | 12 | GeoJSON | Emitting `NaN` or `Infinity` in JSON properties | Violates RFC 8259 JSON syntax; web parsers throw `SyntaxError` | Substitute with `0.0` or `null`. |
825: | 13 | All | Empty `FlightDataset` (`points.is_empty()`) | Exporter crashes with index out-of-bounds | Output valid empty file: CSV header row only, valid empty KML Document, valid empty GPX, or empty FeatureCollection. |
826: | 14 | All | XML special characters (`&`, `<`, `>`, `"`) in flight warning messages | Causes XML parser failure (not well-formed XML) | Escape entities (`&amp;`, `&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&quot;`) or wrap in `<![CDATA[ ... ]]>`. |
